# Experiment Protocol

Use the 2C dataset first. 51 subjects on disk, 3 sessions each, 200 trials/session.
See `docs/EXPERIMENT_PROTOCOL.md` for full detail.

## Experiment A: Cross-subject zero-shot

- Randomly select 41 source subjects for training; remaining 10 are target subjects.
- Train on all 3 sessions of the source subjects.
- Zero-shot test on all 3 sessions of the target subjects.
- Target data must never be used in training (no leakage).
- Repeat the subject-wise split multiple times (e.g. 5-10 seeds) and report mean +/- std.
- Persist each split to a JSON file so runs are reproducible.

## Experiment B: Target-subject fine-tuning

- Start from the model pretrained on 41 source subjects.
- For each target subject: fine-tune on Session 1, test on Session 2 + Session 3.
- Compare these adaptation strategies:
  - zero-shot (no fine-tuning)
  - classifier-only fine-tuning
  - adapter fine-tuning
  - prototype update
  - full-model fine-tuning

## Experiment C: Online adaptation

- Start from the pretrained model, optionally after Session 1 fine-tuning.
- Run online test-then-update (prequential) on Session 2 then Session 3.
- For each trial, in order:
  1. Predict the label.
  2. Output a confidence score.
  3. Record prediction, confidence, and correctness.
  4. Only then update the allowed lightweight modules.
- Allowed online-updated modules:
  - prototype memory
  - adapter
  - confidence calibration head
  - batch-norm statistics (causal update only)
  - classifier head only if supervised labels are available
- Do NOT update the full backbone by default.
- Unlabeled online updates must be confidence-gated (only high-confidence trials).

## Experiment D: Ablations

At minimum: without confidence head, without prototype, without online update,
full-backbone update, without domain alignment, softmax-confidence-only,
and no-confidence-threshold.

## Iron rule

Online learning must NEVER train on a trial before that trial has been evaluated.
Never use a whole session to update the model and then test on the same session.
